# Elegy Acolyte's Void: "if ... a spell was warped this turn" (CR 702.185c). Turn 1 Bot1 casts Elegy Acolyte (Black Lotus
# and Mox Jet; the Lotus having left, a Robot that turn), on turn 3 Tannuk, Steadfast Second (four Mox Rubies: no Robot,
# nothing left and nothing warped). On turn 5 Bot1 does nothing but cast Hill Giant for the warp Tannuk gives: nothing left
# the battlefield as the end step begins, so the warp alone makes the Void true and a second Robot is created.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Elegy Acolyte
Mox Ruby x4
Tannuk, Steadfast Second
Hill Giant
Mountain x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x24

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elegy Acolyte.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Robot Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#3.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#4.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Tannuk, Steadfast Second.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Elegy Acolyte; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Robot Token; Tannuk, Steadfast Second
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#3.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Hill Giant.Cast(Ability: Warp)
Bot1.Pass
[T6 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Exile = Hill Giant
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Jet; Elegy Acolyte; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Robot Token; Tannuk, Steadfast Second; Robot Token
